Learned from, no code taken
---------------------------

  src/sound.c is a stub and contains no ported code. When it is implemented it
  will most likely derive from MAME's sound/multipcm.cpp ((c) Miguel Angel
  Horna) and sound/scsp.cpp, and this file must be updated when it does.

  No MAME source is redistributed here; `ref/` is a local scratch directory
  and is git-ignored.


Everything else
---------------

  MIT — (c) 2026 sp00nz and contributors.

  That covers the parts with no MAME ancestor: the recompiled-code execution
  model (func_table.c, the field-sync frame boundary, interrupt dispatch at
  the field boundary), the on-demand coprocessor scheduler in src/copro.c,
  the ROM loading layer, eeprom.c, platform_sdl.c, and the public API in
